==Esperanto==

===Etymology===
Esperanto ''[[ti-]]'' (demonstrative [[:Category:Esperanto correlatives|correlative]] prefix) + ''[[-al]]'' (correlative suffix of reason)

===Conjunction===
{{eo-head|pos=conjunctions}}

# for [[that]] reason (demonstrative correlative of reason)
#: ''Mi pensas, '''tial''' mi estas.'' &mdash;Renato Kartezio
#:: I think, therefore I am. &mdash;René Descartes
#: {{quote-book
|year=2002
|title=La Sankta Biblio
|section=I Makabeoj 2:59
|passage=Ŝandraĥ, Meŝaĥ kaj Abed-Nego havis fidon; '''tial''' ili estis savitaj el la ardantaj flamoj.
|translation=Ananias, Azarias, and Misael, believed, '''for this reason''', they were saved out of the flame.
|url=http://www.reocities.com/cigneto/apokrifo/1Makabeoj.html#cx02
}}
====Usage notes====
When combined with ''[[ĉi]]'', the adverbial particle of proximity, ''tial ĉi'' means "for this reason".

